{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/9056","createdAt":"2026-10-02T08:21:21Z","decision":"accept_change","decisionDigest":"sha256:971e8f8452ac2a6c91a871bb6b1fce5f78eb2920f0e8adc10516f17447947bd0","decisionId":"rdec-c0882751d407035b6b2e60f7e6607aae","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:55237d54d1aaf6b41a7b9f7b69aebe2b647db6ed1f06e938bd80142ce837f121","packageIdentity":"epkg-a14130b6bd67879accd719c6075aa81ec1d9842cf6cef248ecfeb3170b0a7a9c","prNumber":"9056","reason":"Approve (our GitHub comment, \"good to merge from our side\", re-checked on this mirror). The open() guard answers a superseded caller as cancelled instead of stranding it (#9057), verified end-to-end on a live Omarchy/Quickshell session with the real omarchy-menu-select callers. The head b7bd59c4 writes each answer in its own process, which fixes the shared-Process race a 20-summon burst exposed on the first commit (19 callers stuck on quattro, 7 to 12 on 0b4fe29, 0 on b7bd59c4). Remaining gap, not caused by this PR: the peer-death trigger tracked on #9057 (KI-MENU-REQUEST-LIFECYCLE). Advisory: we cannot approve for the maintainers.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
