{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/9056","createdAt":"2026-10-02T10:28:14Z","decision":"accept_change","decisionDigest":"sha256:91dd47e872f5343c13468ab4cfcec443186208cd60011be47a230b115219542a","decisionId":"rdec-93e570ad5a07b8b7ae5af489c0ae9524","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:55237d54d1aaf6b41a7b9f7b69aebe2b647db6ed1f06e938bd80142ce837f121","packageIdentity":"epkg-a14130b6bd67879accd719c6075aa81ec1d9842cf6cef248ecfeb3170b0a7a9c","prNumber":"9056","reason":"Recommend accepting: a new summon now answers the earlier waiting caller as cancelled instead of leaving it stuck (#9057), and the head b7bd59c4 also fixes the burst race found on the first commit. On a live Omarchy session, a burst of 20 summons left 19 callers stuck on quattro c05d9019, 7 to 12 on the first commit 0b4fe29, and 0 on b7bd59c4, in all 6 runs. The two-summon case exits cleanly, and a real selection still returns its value. A headless regression test for overlapping requests fails on both older trees and passes 8/8 on this head. One gap remains outside this PR: if the menu process dies after a summon, the caller still waits forever (tracked on #9057).","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
